Photorealistic vintage 1960s audiophile medallion, square, straight-on, isolated on a pure flat black background, centered and filling 80 percent of the canvas. One circular object, half precision phonograph turntable, half hand-machined solid brass equipment dial. Rim: heavy warm brushed antique brass bezel with fine engraved tick marks and subtle warm amber edge illumination. Face: deep black shellac 78 RPM gramophone vinyl record with ultra-fine concentric grooves and a spun-brass center boss. On the face, two centered lines of lettering in elegant embossed warm gold script: first line "Killa", second line "YuE" (capital Y, lowercase u, capital E). Lettering very large, clear and legible at tiny sizes. Abbey Road studio atmosphere, warm tungsten lighting, crisp macro focus. No other objects, no extra text, no watermark.
